													"box" : 													{
														"maxclass" : "comment",
														"text" : "- scale minutes to phasor time\n- use go ramp to subdivide phasor\n- use “what” to convert to pulse\n- put in left side of Karplus\n- the right side is pitch\n+22 is lowest pitch added to minutes\n- Send to random range and make it randomly go higher\n- I also changed the go book example and put in scale and timer\n\nThere should be a scale 01 to 150 because it’s being multiplied by the original pitch and you can’t multiply by zero or you won’t get a pitch. For example, if the clocks were at zero minutes, I had 22 that pushes the pitch up to 22 and they could multiply times any number between one and 50 so 50×22 is gonna give you a really high frequency.",
